{"kind":"request","text":"Export a guard for item effects from `packages/derive`, so an adapter does not copy the list of effect names.\n\nFiled 2026-11-13 06:59 EST at Hugh's request, from the dap-foldkit M2 rework. Every dap fact below is read at main `64112e45`.\n\n## Ask\n\nExport `isItemEffect(effect: Effect): effect is ItemEffect` beside the type `ItemEffect` in `packages/derive/src/item-effects.ts`. Tie the guard to the type, so that a change to the members of `ItemEffect` without the same change to the guard fails to compile.\n\n## Why\n\n`changeItem` takes an `ItemEffect`. `ItemEffect` is `Extract\u003cEffect, { effect: \"state\" | \"party\" | \"ref\" | \"value\" | \"list\" | \"hold\" }\u003e`. A caller that holds the effects of an entry or of a judged draft must narrow each effect before it calls `changeItem`. dap exports the type and no guard.\n\nThe dap-foldkit replica applies the effects of a member's pending act over the confirmed items with dap's own `newItem` and `changeItem`. It picks the item effects with a hand copy of the six names (`~/play/dap-foldkit/lib/replica/shown.ts`, `ITEM_EFFECTS`). The copy is a set of strings. A seventh item effect in dap compiles in every adapter, and the pending change then does not show. Inside dap, `packages/derive/src/fold.ts:117` names the same six in a typed `switch`, which the compiler checks. An adapter has no such check.\n\n## Optional second part\n\nThe replica also lists the items that an entry changed, to publish them. It reads `\"item\" in effect` for that (`lib/replica/replica.ts`, `fold`). That test also matches `relation`, whose `item` is an item of the owner's scope, and `attention`. The read of `state.item(id)` hides the error today. If `applyEntry` returned the local IDs of the items that it changed, the replica would read no effect to publish a change. The planner decides whether this part is worth a change to the signature of `applyEntry`. The guard alone closes this request.\n\n## Size and priority\n\nSmall: one exported function, one compile-time tie to the type, one test. Low priority. No dap-foldkit milestone waits for it. It belongs with PG-1 `cb07b59b`, before the replica moves into `packages/client`.\n\n## Filing rule\n\nThe request adds no scope kind, no platform definition name, no capability, no tool family and no record model. It exports a guard for a type that is already public.\n\nSource: `~/play/dap-foldkit/PLAN.md`, draft 3, revision 5, section 8.3, row D8.","body":{"conditions":"isItemEffect is exported from @generalbusiness/dap-derive beside ItemEffect; a change to the members of ItemEffect without the same change to the guard fails to compile; one test covers each member and one effect that is not an item effect; the planner records whether applyEntry returns the changed item IDs; npm run gate passes.","target":"inherit","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}